    "### 3.4 Feature engineering: create new, more informative columns\n",
    "\n",
    "**What this cell does**: builds new columns by combining existing ones.\n",
    "\n",
    "| New feature | Idea |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `TotalSF` | total surface = basement + 1st floor + 2nd floor |\n",
    "| `TotalBath` | full baths + 0.5 × half baths (including the basement) |\n",
    "| `TotalPorchSF` | all porches and decks added up |\n",
    "| `HouseAge`, `RemodAge` | age at sale time (the price depends on age *when sold*, not on the year number) |\n",
    "| `IsRemodeled`, `IsNew` | simple yes/no flags |\n",
    "| `QualSF` | quality × living area: a big house **and** well built is worth much more than the sum of both |\n",
    "| `HasPool`, `Has2ndFloor`, `HasGarage`, `HasBsmt`, `HasFireplace` | presence flags |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why**: models only see the columns we give them. A linear model cannot invent \"total surface\" by itself. **This step is usually where most of the improvement comes from** on this competition.\n",
    "\n",
    "`.clip(lower=0)` avoids negative ages (a few houses were sold before the recorded build year)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 127,
   "id": "4ab50c7b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Columns now: 92\n"
     ]
