   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**What this cell does**: defines the 6 models in a dictionary, trains each one on the 80% part (`fit`) and evaluates it on the 20% validation part. The result is shown as a table, best RMSLE highlighted.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What to look for**: plain Linear Regression is usually clearly worse (overfitting with so many columns). Regularised models and boosting do much better. Compare also MAE in dollars: it is the most intuitive figure."
   ]
