    "### 4.4 Seeing regularisation in action\n",
    "\n",
    "**What this cell does**: trains Ridge and Lasso with several fixed α values and reports (a) how many weights Lasso keeps non-zero and (b) the validation RMSLE.\n",
    "\n",
    "**How to read it**\n",
    "- **Lasso**: as α grows, more weights are forced to exactly 0 (the model uses fewer columns). With a tiny α it keeps nearly everything and can overfit; with a huge α it keeps almost nothing and **underfits** (RMSLE explodes).\n",
    "- **Ridge**: weights shrink but are never exactly 0 (see the \"average |weight|\" column).\n",
    "- The best RMSLE is somewhere in the middle: **that sweet spot is what `LassoCV` / `RidgeCV` find automatically.**"
   ]
  },
