    "# Part 6 — Tuning and ensembling\n",
    "\n",
    "## 6.1 Hyperparameter tuning with `GridSearchCV`\n",
    "- **Parameters** are what a model learns by itself (e.g. the weights).\n",
    "- **Hyperparameters** are the settings **we** choose *before* training (`learning_rate`, `max_depth`, α…).\n",
    "\n",
    "`GridSearchCV` tries **every combination** from a grid we define, scores each with cross-validation, and keeps the best. It is like testing every recipe variant and keeping the tastiest — an automated, fair way to choose settings.\n",
    "\n",
    "Cost grows fast: 2 × 3 × 2 = 12 combinations × 3 folds = 36 trainings. (For Ridge/Lasso/ElasticNet we do not need it: their `…CV` versions already tune α.)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fe21e6a3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**What this cell does**: tunes Gradient Boosting over 12 combinations of `learning_rate`, `max_depth` and `min_samples_leaf` (the minimum number of houses in a leaf: bigger = simpler trees, less overfitting). It prints the best combination, and keeps the best model in `best_gb`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 171,
   "id": "772a9e7d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Fitting 3 folds for each of 12 candidates, totalling 36 fits\n",
      "Best settings: {'learning_rate': 0.05, 'max_depth': 2, 'min_samples_leaf': 5}\n",
      "Best CV RMSLE (3-fold): 0.1124\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "param_grid = {\n",
    "    \"learning_rate\": [0.02, 0.05],\n",
    "    \"max_depth\": [2, 3, 4],\n",
    "    \"min_samples_leaf\": [5, 15],\n",
    "}\n",
    "gb_to_tune = GradientBoostingRegressor(n_estimators=600, max_features=\"sqrt\", subsample=0.7,\n",
    "                                       loss=\"huber\", random_state=random_state)\n",
    "\n",
    "grid = GridSearchCV(gb_to_tune, param_grid, cv=3, scoring=\"neg_root_mean_squared_error\", n_jobs=-1, verbose=1)\n",
    "grid.fit(X, y)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Best settings:\", grid.best_params_)\n",
    "print(f\"Best CV RMSLE (3-fold): {-grid.best_score_:.4f}\")\n",
    "best_gb = grid.best_estimator_"
   ]
