    "### Saving the model with `joblib`\n",
    "\n",
    "**What this cell does**: saves the trained model (and the list of columns it expects) in a file, then reloads it and checks it gives identical predictions.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why**: training can take minutes; once saved, any other program (a web app, an API) can load the model and predict instantly **without retraining**. Note: new houses must go through the same preparation steps (Part 3) before being given to the model."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1e7e5640",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "joblib.dump({\"model\": final_model, \"columns\": list(X.columns)}, \"final_model.joblib\")\n",
    "\n",
    "loaded = joblib.load(\"final_model.joblib\")\n",
    "same = np.allclose(loaded[\"model\"].predict(X_test), final_model.predict(X_test))\n",
    "print(\"Model saved to final_model.joblib | reload gives identical predictions:\", same)"
   ]
